From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:28:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/21] wifi: ath12k: keep peach DMA inside the low 256 MiB

Coherent allocations for PCI 0x110e came out at the top of the
32-bit space. Stock's peach window is the low 384 MiB. A 28-bit
mask puts the firmware segments in that range.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
index 6441927b5..666eb48d2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -860,9 +860,21 @@ static int ath12k_pci_claim(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci, struct pci_dev *pdev)
 		goto disable_device;
 	}
 
-	ab_pci->dma_mask = DMA_BIT_MASK(ATH12K_PCI_DMA_MASK);
+	/* Peach firmware memory landed at the top of the 32-bit DMA
+	 * space (0xfe400000 and up). Stock's window is the low
+	 * 384 MiB. Keep this chip's DMA inside that.
+	 */
+	if (device_id == 0x110e)
+		ab_pci->dma_mask = DMA_BIT_MASK(28);
+	else
+		ab_pci->dma_mask = DMA_BIT_MASK(ATH12K_PCI_DMA_MASK);
 	dma_set_mask(&pdev->dev, ab_pci->dma_mask);
-	dma_set_coherent_mask(&pdev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	if (device_id == 0x110e) {
+		dma_set_coherent_mask(&pdev->dev, ab_pci->dma_mask);
+		ath12k_info(ab, "pci dma mask %d bits\n", 28);
+	} else {
+		dma_set_coherent_mask(&pdev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	}
 
 	pci_set_master(pdev);
 
